From: illogical-impulse <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/lock: destroy surfaces before removed outputs

Qt emits screenRemoved while the disappearing QWaylandScreen and wl_output
are still alive. Deferring WlSessionLockSurface deletion until the next event
loop iteration lets Qt release that wl_output first, leaving the native lock
surface attached to a stale protocol object.

Destroy the wrapper synchronously in the screen-removal callback. Its
destructor immediately destroys the QWindow's native Wayland resources while
leaving deletion of the QQuickWindow object itself deferred.
---
 src/wayland/session_lock.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp b/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
index 1ae8d2e..1c94471 100644
--- a/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ void WlSessionLock::updateSurfaces(bool show, WlSessionLock* old) {
 	for (auto& [screen, surface]: map) {
 		if (!screens.contains(screen)) {
 			this->surfaces.remove(screen);
-			surface->deleteLater();
+			delete surface;
 		}
 	}
 
